+### The backdrop
+
+The backdrop is `frontend/public/hero-backdrop.svg`, and it is **drawn by
+`tools/make-hero-backdrop.mjs`** (29 Oct 2026): edit the script and run it, never
+the SVG. `node tools/make-hero-backdrop.mjs --check` exits 1 when the file on
+disk is not what the script draws. It replaced a photo, `hero-backdrop.jpeg`,
+whose source was never recorded; there is no copy of the backdrop in this folder
+any more, so for a deck open the SVG in a browser and export from there.
+
+Note the file is the **raw drawing**. On the page it is composited: 0.40 opacity
+in light mode with `brightness(0.5) saturate(2.6) contrast(0.91)`, and 0.26
+opacity in dark. So it looks considerably more muted on the landing page than it
+does on its own. Those numbers are tuned against the contrast of the hero copy
+sitting on top of it — see the note above the filter in `index.css` before
+changing any of them.
